# XR Workspace: the VITURE Luma Ultra. Not installed by anything here: docs/usb-drops.md has the commands, and removing this file
# undoes it.
#
# Access. The driver package's 70-viture-xr.rules matches ACTION=="add" only, so on a boot with the glasses already plugged in the
# "bind" event that follows clears the uaccess tag, and logind never gives the user the device: "Cannot open device, may not
# connect", then a segfault in the SDK. Measured 2026-11-03: TAGS=:uaccess:seat: but CURRENT_TAGS=:seat:. Upstream issue #129's
# workaround is the same bug. This rule has no ACTION, so the tag survives every event.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="35ca", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"

# Power. The glasses' own hub and its tracking device never suspend. Not the cause as far as anyone can tell (the hub was never
# seen suspended, and the disconnects are clean), but one thing fewer to wonder about. The camera is left alone: nothing here uses
# it, and suspended it draws less.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTR{idProduct}=="8091", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="35ca", ATTR{idProduct}=="1104", ATTR{power/control}="on"
